      "text": "## The Big Picture"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#002",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:00-overview, git-history:hvac:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "hvac/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "HVAC Systems - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "HVAC is one integrated control problem: move heat where you want it, dilute contaminants\nto acceptable concentration, and maintain moisture in the human comfort band — all while\nspending as little energy as possible. The thermodynamic ceiling is the Carnot bound:"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#003",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:00-overview, git-history:hvac:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "hvac/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "HVAC Systems - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nCARNOT COP BOUNDS (temperatures in Kelvin):\n  Cooling:  COP_max = T_cold / (T_hot − T_cold)\n  Heating:  COP_max = T_hot / (T_hot − T_cold)"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#004",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:00-overview, git-history:hvac:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "hvac/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "HVAC Systems - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Example — residential AC:\n  Cooling to 45°F (280K), rejecting heat at 95°F (308K):\n  COP_max = 280 / (308 − 280) = 10.0\n  Real split-system AC: COP 3–5 → 30–50% of Carnot"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#005",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:00-overview, git-history:hvac:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "hvac/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "HVAC Systems - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Key insight: COP_max ∝ 1/ΔT — as outdoor T rises (hotter day),\n  ΔT increases, Carnot COP falls, equipment works harder for less effect.\n  This is why sizing and economizer strategies matter.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#006",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
